## 12. Hair v4: three cloths that cost no more than shipped hair, solved offline (2026-10-25) [obs: offline gate on 14 game pose dumps; in-game liveliness pending]

Goal (QA 146): hair cost <= shipped (tifa 7 cloths / 206 particles / 57 collider refs / 1 730 particle x collider pairs; succubus 3 / 84 / 32 / 893; rangiku 5 / 58 / 53 / 942) with less clipping than the m21d3 set
(6 hair + 4 garment cloths, 198 particles, 154 refs, 4 187 pairs). Result `own/bonecloth/deliver_v4c` (README = the numbers): 3 cloths, 117 particles, 505 constraints, 41 refs, 1 417 pairs; offline inside-skin vertices 625 -> 289, deepest 39.9 -> 17.2 mm, spawn push 24 -> 8.5 mm (v4b, the first delivery: 353).
Recipe (all AUTO, `own/bonecloth/v4/`, chains `shion_build/resume/hair_v4_chain.sh <name> <run_solve args>` write `chain_<name>.DONE|.FAIL`, logs `own/logs/hair_v4_chain_*.log`):
1. **Merge by behaviour, not by region**: one cloth per profile family: back panels (asuna:B_HairBack, FixedNonRotation 1), the long strands + chin strands (tifa lifeguard:B_HairFront, FNR 1), bangs + temples + tufts (power:B_HairFront, FNR 0);
   `own_bonecloth.lock_chains` lets several lock regions share one MagicaBoneCloth (`make_plan.py`). 10 cloths -> 3 saves the per-cloth team/job overhead; particles are what the lock cut gives (7 panels x 8, ...).
2. **Collider design is the whole game**: a straight capsule over a curved patch (shoulder, forehead) bulges 15-30 mm and pops the styled hair at spawn; hair-only SPHERE covers (k-means on the skin patch, 3 per shoulder/forehead/face,
   `own_hair_colliders.py` zone shape "sphere") beat capsules (744 vs 464 inside after the same solve), a cone fitted to BreastRest (`shape:"cone"`) hugs the breast. Styled hair can sit INSIDE the body at rest (the body grew after styling:
   BreastRest v2, shoulders): the spawn push then removes real clipping; tailoring (shrinking the collider by the deficit, `hair_solve.py`, `--pop-mm 3`, `--no-tailor cloth:substring@mm`) trades that against pop and costs coverage.
3. **hair_solve grid on the real pose dumps** (`run_solve.py <name> --radius-scales ... --lists ... --colliders-cfg ... --colliders-json ...`): particle radius x1.25 won (x0.6 / 0.8 / 1.0 / 1.25 / 1.5 = 954 / 746 / 464 / 349 / 298 inside; x1.5 deeper and more push);
   a smaller radius for the bangs (x0.45/0.65), partial tailoring (<= 10 mm) and a looser Long cloth were not better (369-478); leaving the Long cloth untailored gives 337 but 14.6 mm push.
3b. **Per cloth class collider allowance (the biggest single gain)**: the margin of a sphere cover over the skin (`allow_mm` of the zone) must match the cloth: broad back panels (particle radius 22-31 mm) need 12 mm,
   the front hair (radius 12.5 mm, strands only ~10 mm wide) needs 3 mm and MORE spheres: five 3 mm shoulder covers per side (zone copies `lShoulderSphF`, `count 5`) instead of three 12 mm ones took the doggy front-hair clipping from 35 to 4 inside
   (bangs/temples fall on the shoulders; with three big spheres the gaps between the spheres and the 16 mm tailoring left the skin uncovered). The same trick on the back hair (8 mm, five spheres) was worse (+20 inside); on the long strands mixed.
4. **Prune colliders by gate, not by usage** (`prune_eval.py <solve dir> <name> '<json drops>'`, 7 min each): dropping unused spheres (Back lShoulderSph1/rShoulderSph1/lAss/rBreastCone, Long neckHair/head, Front face0/2 + shoulder1/2) cost +4 inside;
   also dropping Back arm/hand colliders cost +200 (hands/forearms matter in sex poses). 57 -> 41 refs.
Pitfalls: a global radius scale moves every cloth; an untailored set has spawn pushes up to 25 mm; usage tables of a collider universe are meaningless (colliders far from a cloth show huge "usage"); `make_deliver_v4.py` must exit non-zero when verify fails
(it ran with a wrong types.cs path for three chains before I noticed: check `ALL_OK` in verify_report.json); the clip gate cannot see the hairline vertices blended to `head_base` (rigid head skin: 10 vertices, 12.7 mm in doggy, same as m21d3).
Liveliness tooling (no plugin needed on the shared rig): `scripts/ingame_test/hair_ab.py run|analyze` (36 transform dumps per actor in one scene -> tip rms / chain length / head drive; the rms of random-phase samples is an unbiased amplitude estimate),
`scripts/hair_param_variant.py <stem.tfa> <variant.tfa> --set '{"B_HairLong": {"restoreRotation": [0.12, 0.03]}}'` (edits MagicaBoneCloth.clothParams of a BUILT stem + clone-rename in seconds: parameter variants without re-assembly).
Shipped long-hair parameter families for variants (`{SHIPPED_LIB~0}/_bonecloth/bonecloth_param_profiles.json`): tifa:B_HairC restoreRotation 0.117->0.038, maxVelocity 1.85->0.71 (clampPositionLength 0.194); asuna:B_HairBack 0.152->0.023 / 1.65->0.72;
irelia:B_HairBack 0.165->0.108 / 1.21; our Long = tifa lifeguard:B_HairFront 0.336->0.083, maxVelocity 1.25->0.31, mass 4.73->2.22 (the stiffest of the long profiles); bangs power:B_HairFront maxVelocity 0.15 (limited by design).
