## 15. Soft-tissue physics through data-only patches: depth rule, spring fit, the neck line (2026-10-26) [obs: decompile 0.5991 + sim port on the exact inputs; in-game turn pending the next build]
**Depth rule** (own_cloth.depth_from_rule, cfg `cloth_virtual_opts[part].depth_rule`, no assembler change): every depth-curved ClothParams value is evaluated per particle at `ClothData.vertexDepthList` (CurveParam.Evaluate = linear start -> end when useCurve is off); BFS level / (max level - 1) is the shipped depth. The rule replaces it by a geodesic ramp from anchor regions
(Ass: Vagina / InsideVagina / Anus / InsideAnus, Breasts: Nipples = areola + nipple) and from the Fixed border, smoothstep, `{"anchor_regions": [...], "ramp_mm": [0, 40], "border_ramp_mm": [0, 20]}`; with `clampPositionLength = {start 0, end L, useEndValue 1}` the ball radius is 0 at the anchors / border (= the shipped pinned behaviour) and L on free tissue.
ClampPositionJob also has an axis box (`clampPositionRatioX/Y/Z`, limits ratio*L per axis in the particle's base rotation frame, LookRotation(normal, tangent): Z = normal) used as the normal-axis cap against clipping through bras / suit shells (3.2 mm breasts, 10 mm butt). Rest state is unchanged (only vertexDepthList + clothParams differ); `physics_bundle.py verify` compares a built bundle with `expected/*.npz`.
**Spring fit** (`own/bonecloth/jiggle/spring_fit.py`): the game step x1 = (x + h v q)(1 - s), s = 1-(1-p)^1.5, q = (1-drag)^1.5, h = 1/60 has eigenvalues r e^(+-i theta): the NATURAL frequency is sqrt(w_d^2 + sigma^2)/2pi, not the visible peak spacing (p 0.14 + drag 0.085 = 4.74 Hz natural, 4.4 Hz damped: the first survey matched the Blender fit 4.37 Hz with the damped value, +8 %). Blender fits (thighs/RESULT.json): butt 4.37 Hz zeta 0.36 -> spring 0.121 drag 0.087; boobs 4.15 Hz zeta 0.21 -> spring 0.116 drag 0.
Amplitude = world influence (inertia coupling k): static response k / w0^2 = 1.33 (butt, k 1) / 1.04 (breasts, k 0.7) mm per m/s2 vs Blender 0.69 / 0.76. The team spring pulls EVERY movable particle back by s per step before ClampPosition (no per-particle weight in SpringJob), so hole particles pushed out by a shaft end the step (1-s) = 82 % displaced: measure hole displacement in game (k ~ 24 mm p99).
**Delivery without touching assemble_own.py**: cfg `class_defaults` -> a directory holding a byte copy of class_defaults.json + the modified cloth_param_profiles.json (the assembler loads the profile set from dirname(class_defaults)); patch `set` replaces WHOLE dict keys (cloth_virtual_opts, cloth_reduce_mm): every patch that sets such a key must carry the identical final dict (physics.json + neck.json are generated together by `physics_build.py`), otherwise the alphabetically last patch silently reverts the others.
`own/bonecloth/jiggle/physics_build.py` (gates on the exact patch inputs of the target cfg, writes physics.json / neck.json / READY_*), `physics_bundle.py stem|verify` and `neck_stem.py` make test stems from a BUILT bundle by data-object edits (seconds, no build), `physics_live.py` is the in-game turn (clips + numeric tracks incl. the outward-excursion clip proxy).
**The neck line (user shot 2026-10-26 15:15)**: the Throat patch of m21f2f/h was the coarse 'T' reduction (cloth_reduce_mm Throat 12, shape tol 9 mm = 165 particles): on-screen error vs the skin 1.0-2.4 mm p99 / up to 3.8 mm in head-turned poses (doggy 2.42/3.81, spread 1.99/3.14, m1b 1.73/2.97; stand 0.08) while its border stays pinned = a step along the border. T2c Throat (reduce 3, tol 2.25 = 953 particles = shipped-class 939): p99 0.13-0.42, max <= 1.9. Rule: a patch profile is only accepted when its ON-SCREEN error in the real head-turned / spread poses is <= the as-built k (section 14.1); the first 'T' profile was accepted on stand + random-pose numbers only. Breasts had the same defect class (reduce 10 = 540 particles) and moved to T2c (2 000).
**Pitfalls**: (1) harness `record` in mode render writes JPEG bytes into files named f_NNNN.png: `ffmpeg -i f_%04d.png` writes a 0-byte mp4 (every clip of that evening); use `scripts/ingame_test/frames_to_mp4.py` (sniffs the codec, deletes a failed 0-byte output). (2) Python text-mode read + `newline=""` write converts a CRLF file to LF: edit CRLF files with newline="" on BOTH sides (or bytes). (3) a tool-call heredoc turns a doubled backslash + n into a real newline inside a Python string: build such strings with chr(92). (4) harness commands do not run while a `record` is active (RecordStep returns first): record and pose switching cannot be interleaved; run clothtrack (plugin, its own channel) in a thread beside the harness commands instead.

